  "plain": "In the 1960s, a wealthy businessman named Floyd Odlum pressed her family into signing an open-ended contract with her father, according to Linda Brown, who tells it as someone who lived through it. She speaks on Jesse Michels's episode with the writer Nick Cook about antigravity craft, and says Odlum \"did force\" the signing. The point of the story is that a powerful backer kept her father's work tied to him with no end date."
